  "grammar_explanations": [
    {
      "slug": "present continuous: affirmative (I'm wearing ...)",
      "title_form": "Presente continuo: afirmativo (I'm wearing ...)",
      "title_target": "Present Continuous: Affirmative (I'm wearing ...)",
      "description_md_form": "Usamos el **presente continuo** para hablar de lo que está pasando **ahora mismo**. Para formar el afirmativo, usamos el verbo **to be** (am/is/are) + el verbo con **-ing**.\n\n- **I'm wearing** a black shirt. = Estoy llevando una camisa negra.\n- **She's wearing** a white dress. = Ella está llevando un vestido blanco.\n\nLa forma corta (I'm, She's) es la más común al hablar. ¡Es muy fácil! Solo recuerda: **to be + verbo-ing**.",
      "description_md_target": "We use the **present continuous** to talk about what is happening **right now**. To form the affirmative, we use the verb **to be** (am/is/are) + the verb with **-ing**.\n\n- **I'm wearing** a black shirt.\n- **She's wearing** a white dress.\n\nThe short form (I'm, She's) is the most common when speaking. It's very easy! Just remember: **to be + verb-ing**.",
      "grammar_structure": "Subject + to be (am/is/are) + verb-ing",
      "conjugation_table": {
        "name": "present_continuous_affirmative",
        "headers": [
          "Pronombre",
          "To be",
          "Verbo -ing",
          "Ejemplo"
        ],
